// TEST: A literal returned through a leading opaque RaggedIdx annotation is refused (rejects)
// ============================================================================
// Gap G190 (a), Codex diff review of A4: the let-annotation refusal of
// index-types/579 missed a literal that gets the type through a function
// RETURN annotation -- the interpreter read it as a plain array, and the C++
// lane returned a ragged view over the callee's automatic storage. The
// refusal now sits where every literal has its final type (zonk): returns,
// blocks and tuple components alike (index-types/581).
// ============================================================================
function f() -> Array<Float64 like RaggedIdx<_>, Idx<1>> = [[1.0], [2.0]]
let a = f()
let x = a(0, 0)
// ERROR: BL4003
// ERROR-CONTAINS: has no outer axis for its row lengths to vary over
// REJECT-AT: lower
